{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789401626,"nonce":"dpvspJOmNG1Tf3NMl+TZreZg+zw=","title":"A fiber that yields from compiled code resumes with another activation's JIT state","message":"The thread's JitContext (module variables, closure, defining class,\nfunction id) and JIT depth are per activation, saved and restored by\nthe dispatch helpers around calls but not around a fiber switch.\nFiber A yields from inside a compiled closure body; the host resumes\nfiber B, whose compiled activation installs its own context; A is\nresumed and reads B's closure through wren_load_jit_closure — the\nwrong upvalues. hatch-proc's \"two fibers reading different processes\ninterleave\" hung or read \"\" once the yielding closure compiled; the\nsame shape is what 6450b64 saw at --jit-threshold 1.\n\ntry_krio_yield now saves the context and depth before the switch and\nreinstalls them when the fiber resumes; try_krio_call does the same\nfor the caller around the resume. Regression test\ne2e_compiled_bodies_yield_from_fiber_stacks.","files":null}]}